WEBVTT

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:07.707 line:92%,end size:91%
A karyotype tells us which chromosomes a cell has, how
many copies there are, and whether their structure has
changed.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.670 line:92%,end size:91%
That can help diagnose genetic disorders and some
cancers.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:17.180 line:92%,end size:91%
When a living cell divides, can we see where an
abnormal chromosome count comes from?

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.780 line:92%,end size:91%
We lack a general way to label chromosome identities
through mitosis.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.796 line:92%,end size:91%
ChromoWorld brings two streams together. Fixed cells
provide the reference identities.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:34.535 line:92%,end size:91%
ChromoPix identifies them, and ChromoLift builds a
three-dimensional reference atlas.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:42.073 line:92%,end size:91%
ChromoPose separates live instances. Tracking links
them. ChromoID matches their shapes.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:50.694 line:92%,end size:91%
G-banding shows stripes on dehydrated chromosomes. In
rehydrated FISH images, the stripes disappear and
shapes become more varied.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:56.720 line:92%,end size:91%
All three models train on G-banding alone. Each loses
accuracy when tested on FISH.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:04.709 line:92%,end size:91%
In this FISH field, Mask R-CNN finds no instances. Both
YOLO models draw masks, but assign incorrect chromosome
identities.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:11.600 line:92%,end size:91%
FISH brings us closer. Rehydrated chromosomes lack
bands, but DNA probes can identify them.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.155 line:92%,end size:91%
Probe labels are precise, but sparse within a field.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:25.366 line:92%,end size:91%
ChromoPix learns from the labels and from paired views
of the same chromosome. One view keeps the shape while
suppressing fine texture.

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:33.648 line:92%,end size:91%
Aligning their features rewards what survives that
change. A chromosome-class prompt lets the decoder
focus on one identity at a time.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:40.157 line:92%,end size:91%
We tested ChromoPix across four cell lines. The F1
scores stay in a similar range.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:48.620 line:92%,end size:91%
Changing the field of view changes apparent scale.
Performance holds up better under moderate rescaling.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.508 line:92%,end size:91%
Rotating or flipping the test images barely changes
performance.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.544 line:92%,end size:91%
Increasing crowding or blur makes the task harder.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:08.615 line:92%,end size:91%
Here, FISH labeled this smaller instance as chromosome
one. ChromoPix called it chromosome seventeen, flagging
the assignment for review.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.657 line:92%,end size:91%
Now follow one chromosome where the assignments agree.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:19.026 line:92%,end size:91%
We measure one tagged chromosome, then use UMAP to
place its shape at a point.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:33.331 line:92%,end size:91%
Pull back to more than seven hundred thousand
chromosome instances. Each point has a shape, and its
color marks a chromosome class.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:41.795 line:92%,end size:91%
Across both preparations, the classes follow a similar
order. Can those relationships carry over to living
cells?

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:49.305 line:92%,end size:91%
Whole-cell projections can collapse identities. Better
views recover only part of the order.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.820 line:92%,end size:91%
First, separate the chromosomes in three dimensions.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:59.620 line:92%,end size:91%
Here FAST-CHIMP produces many small fragments.
Cellpose-SAM shows broader, joined-looking regions.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.780 line:92%,end size:91%
ChromoPose better preserves long, separate shapes in
this frame.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:12.600 line:92%,end size:91%
To follow a bend, ChromoPose first uses predicted
distance and flow to move voxels toward the local
centerline.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:18.903 line:92%,end size:91%
Then it follows the learned flow along the bend. Voxels
that converge together form one instance.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:29.731 line:92%,end size:91%
Tracking links those three-dimensional instances across
frames. Their measured shapes become the input for
chromosome identification.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:40.955 line:92%,end size:91%
A live chromosome provides its own training pair: its
projection and its measured three-dimensional shape,
including volume, elongation, and sphericity.

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:51.405 line:92%,end size:91%
ChromoLift learns that mapping with flow matching. It
moves compact shape descriptors, so thousands of
labeled references can be lifted in batches.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:59.180 line:92%,end size:91%
ChromoID compares each live instance with class
prototypes from the lifted reference atlas.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:02.739 line:92%,end size:91%
It then assigns identity slots jointly within the cell.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:14.650 line:92%,end size:91%
The class centers nearly overlap after direct
projection. Optimal views separate them partly. With
ChromoLift and ChromoID, the class order becomes
clearer.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:20.268 line:92%,end size:91%
We can compare the reviewed chromosome three candidates
with the measured fluorescence.

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:27.443 line:92%,end size:91%
For chromosome eighteen, the tag also lets us check
where the candidates sit over time.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:38.117 line:92%,end size:91%
In patient-derived tumor cells, imaging suggested that
one daughter received two copies of chromosome fourteen
and the other received four.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.951 line:92%,end size:91%
We isolated daughter cells and grew them into separate
clones.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.364 line:92%,end size:91%
Copy-number differences persisted across passages.

00:04:54.290 --> 00:05:01.447 line:92%,end size:91%
Higher-copy clones showed stronger AKT signaling and
greater sensitivity to capivasertib in the lab.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:07.575 line:92%,end size:91%
The clinical team independently chose capivasertib with
endocrine therapy.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:13.607 line:92%,end size:91%
Liver target lesions shrank by nearly a third at eight
weeks, and by nearly half at eighteen.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:22.568 line:92%,end size:91%
Tumor markers and liver biochemistry improved. Daily
function improved too, with less liver pain and
fatigue.

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:32.125 line:92%,end size:91%
Reading chromosome identities in living cells lets us
ask what an unequal division sets in motion.
